# Willo backend runtime configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env` for local development. Never commit `.env`.

# Core ------------------------------------------------------------------------
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=4200

# REQUIRED. The Postgres this server actually opens. This value pairs with
# `bun run db:up` (docker-compose.postgres.yml), which starts a local Postgres
# with matching user/password/database.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://willo:willo@127.0.0.1:5433/willo_dev

# Oxy platform ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Base URL of the Oxy API. `requireOxyAuth`/`getRequiredOxyUserId` (both from
# @oxy.so/core/server) validate every request's bearer token by calling out to
# this API with the token the client sent — there is no local signing secret
# to configure, and no other Oxy-specific credential this service needs.
OXY_API_URL=https://api.oxy.so

# Cross-origin access -----------------------------------------------------------
# Comma-separated browser origins allowed to call this API with credentials,
# in addition to the built-in *.oxy.so family that createOxyCors always
# allows. The deployed web app lives at https://willo.sh; add your local dev
# origin(s) too (e.g. http://localhost:8081 for `expo start --web`).
CORS_ORIGINS=https://willo.sh,http://localhost:8081

# Device pairing (Willo Local, OxyHQ/Willo#9) ------------------------------------
# REQUIRED to issue or complete a device-initiated tunnel claim
# (POST /tunnel/claim, POST /homes/:id/claim-device) — encrypts the tunnel
# secret at rest for the brief window it sits in device_claims.pending_secret
# between an owner completing a claim and the device's own next poll
# collecting it. 64 hex characters (32 bytes). Generate with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
TUNNEL_CLAIM_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# Ecosystem-activity telemetry (optional) ----------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL. Both must be set for src/ecosystemActivity.ts to publish this
# service's traffic to Oxy; with either missing (the default until Oxy
# registers an application for Willo) it disables itself with a warning and
# the server runs exactly as before. No separate enable flag — presence of
# both credentials is the only switch.
# OXY_SERVICE_API_KEY=
# OXY_SERVICE_API_SECRET=
